# Secrets only — all non-secret configuration lives in config.json (local dev)
# or NOTION_SKILLS_* repo variables (the deployed GitHub Action).
# See config.json.example for the full config structure.

# GitHub push token. If unset, the tool falls back to `gh auth token`.
# Needs push access to the target repo.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx

# Notion API token. `ntn` reads it from the env (overrides keychain auth).
# NOTION_API_TOKEN=ntn_xxx

# Any config.json field can also be supplied/overridden via its NOTION_SKILLS_*
# env var (env wins over config.json). This is how the GitHub Action runs with
# no committed config.json. See CONFIG_ENV_VARS in src/config.ts, e.g.:
# NOTION_SKILLS_DATA_SOURCE_ID=...
# NOTION_SKILLS_GITHUB_REPO=owner/name
